--- with the floating-point licences: fp_contract off, fp_reassociate off, fp_finite_math off ---
--- leg 0: the oracles discriminate ---
the four cumulative sums of the integer input differ pairwise: true
the integer input's partial sums are exact in f32: true
the gradient's partial sums are exact in f32: true
the suffix sums of the weights differ from their prefix sums: true
--- leg 1: puzzle 7 under a training step ---
composed: no scan in the step: true
composed: the step writes the n x n selector: true
rewritten: one forward scan (the cumsum) in the step: true
rewritten: one backward scan (its adjoint, a suffix sum) in the step: true
rewritten: the step writes no n x n node: true
the raw step, ahead of the tier, holds no scan: true
rewritten y equals the composed y bitwise: true
rewritten y equals the host prefix sums: true
rewritten x.grad equals the composed x.grad bitwise: true
rewritten x.grad equals the host suffix sums plus the second contribution: true
a sibling lowering of the rewritten step hits the analysis cache: true
non-dyadic: rewritten y matches the composed y within 1e-6 relative: true
non-dyadic: rewritten x.grad matches the composed x.grad within 1e-5 relative: true
--- leg 2: frontend variants ---
