--- leg 4: near misses are left alone ---
a shifted triangle (r <= q + 1): left alone: true
a band (r <= q and q - r < 3): left alone: true
an anti-triangle (r + q <= n - 1): left alone: true
a mask varying with the row: left alone: true
a singleton extent: left alone: true
mismatched extents: left alone: true
a payload that reads the output position: left alone: true
two reduced loops: left alone: true
a selector with a second writer: left alone: true
an f16 index grid past 2048: left alone: true
a max over a multiplicative 0/1 mask (its zeros are not neutral): left alone: true
an integer target (an f32 state would round its sums): left alone: true
a rejected arm that is zero only before f32 rounding: left alone: true
staged code ahead of the reduction (it may write what the proof read): left alone: true
a copy unfolded through a definition written after the copy: left alone: true
a min whose rejected cells are 0, not +inf: left alone: true
--- leg 5: an infinite payload ---
rewritten: the prefix before the infinity is the finite cumulative sum: true
rewritten: every sum from the infinity on is +inf: true
